WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.416 --> 00:00:02.250
When people ask you what happened here,

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:04.833
tell them King James still rules the East.

00:00:05.166 --> 00:00:08.000
Also, tell them I'm better than Michael Jordan.

00:00:11.333 --> 00:00:13.041
He said what?

00:00:15.375 --> 00:00:17.666
Your generation is soft with your

00:00:17.666 --> 00:00:19.916
load management and your analytics 

00:00:19.916 --> 00:00:21.833
and your AAU Superhouses.

00:00:21.833 --> 00:00:25.375
The Gods of the game will not stand for this.

00:00:25.375 --> 00:00:28.291
A reckoning is coming.

00:01:22.666 --> 00:01:23.708
Hello old friend!

00:01:24.208 --> 00:01:26.791
Ah, Ser Dwyane. Welcome to the Mediadel.

00:01:26.791 --> 00:01:27.708
Thank you.

00:01:27.708 --> 00:01:29.500
I’m so delighted to be teammates again. 

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:31.416
Likewise. We need you.

00:01:31.416 --> 00:01:32.875
We’re a man down without Chuck.

00:01:32.916 --> 00:01:34.541
Wait, what? Where is Ser Charles?

00:01:34.541 --> 00:01:35.750
He’s like the funniest guy on the sh-

00:01:36.458 --> 00:01:37.666
...I mean...well,

00:01:37.666 --> 00:01:39.041
Well, luckily I’m ready to go.

00:01:39.083 --> 00:01:41.000
I’ve actually prepared a bit.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.625
It’s called ‘Wade’s Grades.’ You see, it—

00:01:42.625 --> 00:01:43.666
Woah woah, slow down, chief.

00:01:43.666 --> 00:01:46.416
You can’t be on the show until you’ve earned your press pass.

00:01:46.416 --> 00:01:49.041
Press pass? How do I get a press pass?

00:01:49.041 --> 00:01:50.000
You audition.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.375
An audition? I’m Dwyane Wade!

00:01:52.375 --> 00:01:54.500
Don’t worry, they make it easy on ex-knights.

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:56.375
You just do a quick apprenticeship

00:01:56.375 --> 00:01:59.125
and then present your findings to the other maesters.

00:01:59.125 --> 00:02:00.958
You’ll be reporting on an injury.

00:02:00.958 --> 00:02:03.541
Apprentice to Maester Marc Stein 

00:02:03.541 --> 00:02:05.125
in his investigation of an injury

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:07.166
to a horse?

00:02:07.166 --> 00:02:09.375
Oh, I get it. You’re being funny. 

00:02:12.625 --> 00:02:15.708
Four full MCL tears.

00:02:15.708 --> 00:02:18.625
Four full ACL tears.

00:02:18.625 --> 00:02:21.750
Four full Achilles tears.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:23.625
And a full neck tear. 

00:02:24.166 --> 00:02:26.791
Looks like the horse will be out…

00:02:26.791 --> 00:02:27.833
indefinitely. 

00:02:27.875 --> 00:02:29.625
So what happened?

00:02:29.625 --> 00:02:30.375
Foul play?

00:02:30.541 --> 00:02:31.958
My working theory is that 

00:02:31.958 --> 00:02:34.833
Robin Lopez mistook him for a mascot.

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:38.083
I’ve seen that mark before.

00:02:38.083 --> 00:02:40.458
My squire season I think.

00:02:40.458 --> 00:02:42.583
Yes, it’s hand-checking, no?

00:02:42.583 --> 00:02:44.250
Hand-checking?

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:46.333
Don’t be silly, Dwyane. That was banned years ago.

00:02:46.333 --> 00:02:48.041
What was this horse doing when it got hurt?

00:02:48.041 --> 00:02:49.833
Horse things I assume.

00:02:49.833 --> 00:02:51.583
Take this report to the ravenry.

00:02:51.583 --> 00:02:53.291
Make haste. I don’t want to get scooped.

00:02:54.041 --> 00:02:56.958
Um… ravenry… ravenry…

00:02:56.958 --> 00:02:59.708
Oh! Um, excuse me, Maester Wind Horse.

00:02:59.708 --> 00:03:01.041
Ah, Ser Dwyane.

00:03:01.083 --> 00:03:03.125
I’m supposed to take this to the ravenry. 

00:03:03.125 --> 00:03:04.125
Do you know where that is?

00:03:04.125 --> 00:03:06.458
I do. I’m going there now. 

00:03:06.458 --> 00:03:07.458
Come.

00:03:08.208 --> 00:03:09.125
Poor thing.

00:03:09.125 --> 00:03:10.125
Tell me about it.

00:03:10.125 --> 00:03:11.416
A future Hall of Famer 

00:03:11.416 --> 00:03:13.791
serving as an errand boy to Marc Stein...

00:03:13.791 --> 00:03:16.500
I meant the horse. Out indefinitely. 

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:20.125
Seems he paid a heavy price for speaking ill of His Airness.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:21.958
Where did you hear that?

00:03:21.958 --> 00:03:24.000
My little birds are everywhere—

00:03:25.083 --> 00:03:26.833
well...mostly around LeBron,

00:03:26.833 --> 00:03:27.833
but some other places, too—

00:03:27.833 --> 00:03:30.666
Have your little birds told you anything else about this horse?

00:03:30.666 --> 00:03:32.208
I noticed a strange mark.

00:03:32.208 --> 00:03:34.583
No. Since the horse injury,

00:03:34.625 --> 00:03:37.833
my birds from Tor’Onto have become useless. 

00:03:37.833 --> 00:03:40.458
They’re just repeating the same things over and over.

00:03:40.458 --> 00:03:41.958
What kind of things?

00:03:41.958 --> 00:03:44.291
Oh, how knights these days are soft,

00:03:44.291 --> 00:03:46.333
how the '90s were the best,

00:03:46.333 --> 00:03:48.125
how Ser Jordan is the GOAT. 

00:03:48.125 --> 00:03:49.958
Boring old man stuff, really.

00:03:49.958 --> 00:03:51.791
Boring, eh? 

00:03:51.791 --> 00:03:53.291
Could it be related to the Soul Box?

00:03:53.291 --> 00:03:56.791
Hm, I didn’t think to make that connection. 

00:03:56.791 --> 00:03:59.583
But then again, I don’t have your instincts.

00:03:59.583 --> 00:04:01.375
I never played the game. 

00:04:01.416 --> 00:04:02.291
You never played?

00:04:02.291 --> 00:04:06.541
No. Everything I learned about basketball, I learned…

00:04:06.541 --> 00:04:07.541
in here.

00:04:11.625 --> 00:04:13.041
Whoa.

00:04:13.041 --> 00:04:15.166
So many books.

00:04:15.166 --> 00:04:18.833
All the stories, records, recaps, box scores

00:04:18.833 --> 00:04:20.250
and even memes.

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:22.333
They all live here.

00:04:22.333 --> 00:04:24.791
We are this world’s memory, Dwyane.

00:04:24.791 --> 00:04:28.291
Without us, the histories and legends of our Realm

00:04:28.291 --> 00:04:29.500
would all vanish 

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:32.458
like James Harden in a meaningful playoff game.

00:04:32.458 --> 00:04:36.291
Some say if it’s not in here...it never happened.

00:04:36.291 --> 00:04:39.083
Now if you’ll excuse me for one moment, Dwyane,

00:04:39.083 --> 00:04:40.666
I need to grab a book.

00:04:40.666 --> 00:04:41.708
Wait, I can’t come in?

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:44.083
I’m afraid this is very sensitive information.

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:46.416
Only Maesters with a press pass can enter.

00:04:48.041 --> 00:04:49.083
Hello Dwyane.

00:04:50.041 --> 00:04:51.333
Ser Paul.

00:04:51.333 --> 00:04:54.541
There is no more Paul. There is only...

00:04:54.541 --> 00:04:55.541
The Truth.

00:04:56.041 --> 00:04:57.083
Right.

00:04:57.208 --> 00:05:00.375
Now that I am in the media, I see all.

00:05:00.375 --> 00:05:03.458
I know all...and yes,

00:05:03.458 --> 00:05:04.791
I am better than you.

00:05:04.791 --> 00:05:05.875
Um...

00:05:05.875 --> 00:05:07.416
I have to go now.

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:12.750
Is he…?

00:05:14.291 --> 00:05:15.416
All right, let’s go.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.083
Well this looks like a nice place to have

00:05:19.083 --> 00:05:22.083
a long-form, intimate conversation about basketball.

00:05:22.083 --> 00:05:26.208
Ah yes, here is where we do our pondcasts.

00:05:26.875 --> 00:05:28.208
Here we are.

00:05:28.208 --> 00:05:29.541
Whoa.

00:05:29.541 --> 00:05:31.916
Welcome to the ravenry.

00:05:31.958 --> 00:05:34.916
This is where the Mediadel and fanlings connect,

00:05:34.916 --> 00:05:37.000
or some say, even merge.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:39.625
The network of platforms you see represents

00:05:39.625 --> 00:05:43.208
the various localities that make up the greater ‘Social Mediadel,’

00:05:43.208 --> 00:05:46.166
a never-ending conversation between fanlings, 

00:05:46.166 --> 00:05:47.750
scribes and knights. 

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:49.583
You see, until very recently, 

00:05:49.583 --> 00:05:52.125
only those cloaked in Mediadel chains 

00:05:52.125 --> 00:05:54.041
could reach all corners of Balleros.

00:05:54.583 --> 00:05:56.041
But no longer.

00:05:56.041 --> 00:05:57.541
So, what do you have for me?

00:05:57.541 --> 00:05:58.875
I have this injury report

00:05:58.875 --> 00:06:00.958
I’d like to send out from Maester Stein. How do I—

00:06:00.958 --> 00:06:02.666
Horse out indefinitely?

00:06:02.666 --> 00:06:06.125
I broke that 10 minutes ago. Haha!

00:06:06.125 --> 00:06:07.750
Wind Horse, what about you?

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:09.333
Another story about LeBron?

00:06:09.333 --> 00:06:11.291
Those were different times.

00:06:11.333 --> 00:06:15.166
THIS is a story about how Luka Doncic…

00:06:15.166 --> 00:06:16.041
...is the next LeBron.

00:06:16.041 --> 00:06:19.833
-This generation is soft!
-No fundamentals!
-Jordan is the GOAT!

00:06:19.833 --> 00:06:20.916
Wind Horse, look!

00:06:20.916 --> 00:06:23.333
Looks like it’s not just my ravens.

00:06:23.333 --> 00:06:26.541
What in the Seven Hells is going on in Tor’Onto?

00:06:27.333 --> 00:06:30.000
-Jordan is the GOAT!
-This generation is soft!

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.666
Well whatever it is, it seems to have spread.

00:06:32.958 --> 00:06:35.708
Dwyane, we’ve got to get to Cream City!

00:06:35.708 --> 00:06:36.833
I agree—oh wait.

00:06:36.833 --> 00:06:38.458
My audition. It’s tomorrow night.

00:06:38.458 --> 00:06:41.500
Don't worry. I'll get us there in no time.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:43.458
For I am as fast...

00:06:43.458 --> 00:06:44.458
as the wind.

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:48.166
You little mumblecrust,

00:06:48.166 --> 00:06:49.666
I’ll rip your bloody antlers off!!

00:06:49.708 --> 00:06:50.708
Robin, come on, bruv.

00:06:50.708 --> 00:06:52.625
It’s supposed to be play wrestling, ya know?

00:06:52.625 --> 00:06:53.625
This bastard tricked me

00:06:53.625 --> 00:06:55.500
into signing a giant fake contract! 

00:06:58.458 --> 00:06:59.375
What the...

00:07:02.291 --> 00:07:05.416
I ask that you bestow on me the gift of range.

00:07:05.416 --> 00:07:07.000
Please, Jesus...

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:08.000
Shuttlesworth.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:08.791
Giannis!

00:07:08.791 --> 00:07:10.333
Come quick. We’re being attacked.

00:07:10.375 --> 00:07:12.458
Is this some sort of scheduling mistake?

00:07:12.458 --> 00:07:14.416
I didn’t think there was a battle today.

00:07:21.916 --> 00:07:23.708
Wind Horse, look! 

00:07:23.958 --> 00:07:24.791
There's Giannis.

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:31.083
This generation is soft.

00:07:31.083 --> 00:07:33.000
Jordan is the GOAT.

00:07:33.625 --> 00:07:35.000
LeBron is weak.

00:07:35.583 --> 00:07:36.750
Dwyane. Get down.

